invariant: INV-14
file: src/base64_codec.c
catches: scram_test
reason: base64_decode counts a '=' before the last character as padding
  whatever the last character is. "Zg=a" then decodes as "Zg=" does not:
  the call drops the two characters and returns the one byte of "Zg", so
  a second text decodes to the same value, and a character after the
  padding goes unread (RFC 4648 section 3.5). bin/scram_test requires
  CH_EINVAL for "Zg=a".

--- old
    size_t pads = last_is_pad + (last_is_pad & before_is_pad);
--- new
    size_t pads = before_is_pad != 0 ? 2 : last_is_pad;
